{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1110669-technology-and-how-to-use-it","id":1110669,"title":"Technology and how to use it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-02T15:03:45-07:00","id":1110669,"title":"Technology and how to use it?","content":"I'm trying to come with a gadget to use on my libertine.<br /> It is a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hhYPqF3aHUs\" target=\"_blank\">Smart Glasses</a>, one avaiable on the market, with a few upgrades.<br /> <br /> My character created a Algorythm that searches trought Databases online trying to find the person based on it's facial signature.<br /> Once the target is found, a brief confirmation screen appears and them the device starts scanning the peoples public online information.<br /> It browses searching for things like: Name, E-mails, Sites where the person have registered, etc.<br /> <br /> The final result is a clean frame telling the following informations:<br /> Name<br /> Brief Bio<br /> Principal Interests<br /> Most Used Social Network<br /> Important Feed (Like, if the person has been on any newspaper or things like that)<br /> <br /> U guys think that this is like... possible?<br /> If yes, them wich set of mechanics should I use here? The device is not powered by Magic or anything.<br /> <br /> It behaves like a Retainer (Computer searches about people)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T15:12:18-07:00","id":1110671,"title":"","content":"Considering that even zombies and golems use the Retainer rules as a shorthand, I'd say a modified Retainer is the way to go. It'd be highly competent in its field, more than Retainers of its rating are supposed to be, at the cost of being unable to perform actions outside its field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T23:09:44-07:00","id":1110766,"title":"","content":"This just sounds like equipment for an Investigation or Computer action to me, I don't know how many additional mechanics you need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T02:01:20-07:00","id":1110789,"title":"","content":"It's a piece of software that autonomously performs a task almost entirely without user input. The user's skills don't matter, so I think it's much better modeled as a Retainer than an ordinary equipment bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T05:35:31-07:00","id":1110805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1110669-technology-and-how-to-use-it?p=1110789#post1110789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a piece of software that autonomously performs a task almost entirely without user input. The user's skills don't matter, so I think it's much better modeled as a Retainer than an ordinary equipment bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of a flesh and blood personal assistant standing next someone powerful and whispering who each person is as they walk up.<br /> <br /> That person would be a Retainer in game","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T08:18:37-07:00","id":1110859,"title":"","content":"Or a contact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T08:57:06-07:00","id":1110872,"title":"","content":"I see two ways this could be turned into mechanics: <br /> <br /> 1) the software/device is an active thing. It is constantly listening to your desires for it, and feeds you back the information you need proactively. Imagine a dog guarding your house, barking when intruders get nearby. In this case it's acting more like a living entity, and would make a suitable retainer with its own skills in computer and investigation. <br /> <br /> 2) You check in on the software/device and it goes and gathers info and reports to you as a single kind of action. When you're not actively engaging it, it's not really doing anything. (Though in this scenario that could mean you activate it, then come back in ten hours to retrieve the results in an &quot;extended action' sort of way) In this case it's a lot more like a tool than a retainer, and I could see it being an item that gives a bonus to your own investigative/computer skills. <br /> <br /> However you go, it's brilliant for a WoD game. I love it and plan to steal the idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T10:26:59-07:00","id":1110911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1110669-technology-and-how-to-use-it#post1110669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">U guys think that this is like... possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. You're asking your homemade software to do a pretty big piece of data analysis very quickly and then present it in a neat easily usable format. Also, a lot of data is private and a simple piece of software isn't going to be able to access it.<br /> <br /> That said, if you feel it's not too implausible, it probably doesn't matter.. Honestly, whilst it's kinda cool, I'm not entirely sure how useful it'd be. If you want to know somone's interests, why not ask them? (or learn Mind and rip the thoughts directly out of their head)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T10:43:45-07:00","id":1110917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1110669-technology-and-how-to-use-it?p=1110911#post1110911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably not. You're asking your homemade software to do a pretty big piece of data analysis very quickly and then present it in a neat easily usable format. Also, a lot of data is private and a simple piece of software isn't going to be able to access it.<br /> <br /> That said, if you feel it's not too implausible, it probably doesn't matter.. Honestly, whilst it's kinda cool, I'm not entirely sure how useful it'd be. If you want to know somone's interests, why not ask them? (or learn Mind and rip the thoughts directly out of their head)</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, with things like Cheiron, the God-Machine and the assorted mad science hinted at in various books (including the upcoming Deviant) the World of Darkness is clearly more technologically advanced than our reality, so it's not completely out of line for an industrious Libertine to have access to cutting edge near-future tech.<br /> <br /> That said, it's definitely not the sort of thing you just throw together in your garage over the weekend. Obviously it depends on how big of a deal your ST were to make of it, but if this was a request from a player in my game, I'd allow it with the condition that they explained how they got access to the necessary resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T12:15:32-07:00","id":1110943,"title":"","content":"As a wizard it may be easier and more powerful to &quot;magic&quot; the solution. Add some ephemeral thing with a real mind to the Glasses that can interface with it and you're twenty years past where AI currently is. Spirit, Ghost, and Goetia are all valid choices. Ghosts are nice for the human perspective, though Data Spirits are good with information, and Goetia can be very smart especially if it is a literal hacker archetype.<br /> <br /> <b>As a side note:</b> The <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QCOXARv6J9k\" target=\"_blank\">Panopticon</a><sup>*</sup> appreciates the Eye themed surveillance gear you plan to wear, or at least they will when they notice your character.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">*</span>(The link is a relevant movie preview)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-06-2017, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T13:03:16-07:00","id":1112870,"title":"","content":"A Technological Spirit---Familiar or Retainer---could go online and extract the data if it exists there. Call it a Search Daimon or Network Spider.<br /> <br /> Basically, as long as the information exists, you could have a <i>spell</i> go grab it via some sort of sympathetic tie. (and that could simply be a description, if detailed enough.)<br /> Forces could do this, so an Imbued Item could, too. None of this is any less plausible than the Fate spell to dial a number.<br /> <br /> Decide what happens when it <i>cannot</i> be found or the effect fails, though. Also, if something is going online, what happens if it's captured or destroyed? <br /> <br /> <br /> (Mrmdubois: I see what you did there. Contacts, indeed. Heh.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}